WEBVTT

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.360
It was only a month after I
started going to high school.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.370
This is awful.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.700
At the time, I was depressed.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.220
I'd loved two girls so
much I couldn't chose

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.480
between them, and ended
up hurting them both.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.770
I couldn't get over it.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.060
This time, I'll do it right.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.670
This was before I, Ken Sugisaki,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.650
became a member of the Student Council.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.310
This memorial belongs to me.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.130
Episode 0: Sugisaki's Memorial

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.280
Thank you.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.290
Play a love sim!

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.840
A certain person's words gave me the courage

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.220
to try and climb out of the pit I was in,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.030
so I went to a certain store.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.840
Look at all the stuff

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.320
they got since I was last here!

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.830
What should I buy?

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.300
Um, clerk?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.740
Yes? Is something wrong, sir?

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.590
Do you have any recommendations?

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.770
Um... I want to buy a game.
Is there anything you...

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.750
No. Please leave.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.270
Wait a second!

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:40.790
I was just asking which game to buy...

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.590
I've no recommendations.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.540
I don't recommend video
games at all, actually.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.480
Minase-san, you supposedly
work here, right?

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.300
I don't "supposedly" work here.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.300
I do, in fact, work here.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:55.970
Is that a problem?

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.440
Um...

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.600
Is there something else?

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.000
I'm not up to date on games,
so I'd appreciate

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.050
any information
you can give me!

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.950
What kind of information?

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.950
Like what sells best!

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:15.950
Tetris.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.290
I'm sorry for not specifying earlier,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.230
but something in the realm of H-games.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.710
Oh, games for losers who can't
get girlfriends, you mean.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.050
Over here, then.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:33.740
Hey!

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:35.930
Here.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.980
I'm grateful you showed
me where it was,

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.220
but I don't think you're quite
right about these games.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.210
What do you mean?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.070
So what's my best option?

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.490
"Reality" would be my suggestion.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.330
You may be right,
but if you're working here,

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.660
you could at least try
to answer my question!

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.220
Very well.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.500
Then what about this?

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.830
Of course, I've never played it.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.770
But it has a very solid reputation.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.790
Yes... Yes, that's what
I wanted to hear.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.610
It also has a twist ending

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.010
where you discover
the hero is the criminal.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.270
The last scene, where the
heroine is shot and dies,

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.820
is very moving.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.550
That's <i>not</i> what I wanted to hear!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.100
I thought I should explain why
it was held in high regard.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.020
You didn't have to go that far!

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.170
Damn! It sounds really good, too!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.860
I've managed to promote a game so well

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.400
that I've moved a customer to tears.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.800
Sir, may I now call
myself a Master Clerk?

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.580
No! You may not!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.970
Let's try this again, without spoilers!

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.520
Very well.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.230
How about this one?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.400
It's been rather popular, recently.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.230
The girls are drawn pretty well...

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.430
Okay, I'll take it!

00:03:55.430 --> 00:04:00.300
It won the "Worst Game
of the Year" award.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.700
Don't recommended it, then!

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.960
That's not a nice tone
to take with a Master Clerk.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.700
I told you not to call yourself that!

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:10.150
Never mind.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.760
I'll find one myself.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.440
You should've done that
in the first place.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.780
Everyone is your Girlfriend

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.790
A harem end, where everyone is happy?

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.920
I've decided.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.060
From now on, I'm going
to be the kind of hero

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.680
who's popular and gets good grades!

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.130
Morning, everyone.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.300
How are you doing?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.840
My classmates were startled by
the sudden change in my personality.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.530
Some complained.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.390
I apologized for my attitude thus far.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.990
And so, little by little,
I became friends with my class,

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.320
and the days became more fun.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.950
But I wanted something
I could focus on.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.530
It didn't matter what.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.360
I wanted to be someone
I could be proud of.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:18.310
And so I found myself starting
to try for the student council.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.700
Hekiyou Academy's Student
Council has five members.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.980
Four are chosen by popular vote,

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.320
and the fifth is whoever earns

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.650
the highest grades on final exams.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.260
It's called the special slot.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.350
Special Slot

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.820
Are you trying to get the special slot?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.590
What year are you?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.790
A first year.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.030
I see.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.100
You're trying to get the
special slot as a first year.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.220
Um... I'm not really set on it.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:55.390
Unless you're set on
it, you shouldn't try.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.330
It's insulting, actually.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.280
It not as easy as it is
in those H-Games you like.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.520
The girl from the game store!

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.340
You should be quiet in the library.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.720
What is it?

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.480
Have you picked me as
your game girlfriend?

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.060
Mr. H-Game Buyer.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.800
I have not!

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.610
I mean...

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.800
You're a student here?

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.350
You found my school.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.960
I'll have to hire a bodyguard, won't I?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.550
You need to change your opinion of me!

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.050
I need to what?

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:37.810
Um...

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:44.430
Minase-san... Are you perhaps
a second or third year?

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.560
You've finally noticed, Mr. H-Gamer?

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.250
It's Sugisaki!

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.700
So you're an upperclassman!

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.960
I'm sorry I was so rude.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.740
I appreciate people who
are willing to apologize.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:59.350
I forgive you, first year Sugisaki.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.570
Thank you.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.990
As a fellow first year,
I hope we can get along.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.840
You're the same year as me!

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.080
There's a sex criminal in my grade!

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.350
What exactly <i>is</i> your
opinion of me, anyway?

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.170
Number one...

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.590
Heck yes!

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:17.090
...on my "I'd rather stab myself

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.890
than have him as a boyfriend" list.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:19.920
Never mind!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.910
Actually, you're in second place.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.880
I didn't need the follow up!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.270
But who's number one?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.650
Farewell, then.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.080
Wait a second!

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.180
What is it?

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.440
Why don't you want me trying
for the special slot?

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:36.440
I'm just recommending it out
of the goodness of my heart.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.580
You call wrecking someone's
dreams "goodness"?

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:44.150
I hoped I could persuade you
not to waste your time.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.150
Is it weird that I'd try
for the special slot?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:53.080
The freshman at the top of our class...
Do you know what their grades are?

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.030
No... I don't.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.250
They're perfect.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.430
They have a perfect
score in every subject.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:07.990
Perfect, huh?

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:12.270
Well, sometimes flukes... miracles
like that can happen, yeah...

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:15.680
I'm sorry, but it wasn't a fluke.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.750
And they'll stay perfect,

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:23.790
so you should stop trying
for the special slot.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:24.700
Goodbye.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.260
H-How?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.270
How do you know?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:37.000
Because I'm the one with the
best grades. Minase Runa.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.310
Soon, midterms were held.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.430
They were the best
grades I'd ever gotten.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:55.210
Midterm Score: 465   Class Rank: 23 of 234

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.820
But since I was after the special slot,
Midterm Score: 465   Class Rank: 23 of 234

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.300
But since I was after the special slot,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.080
"good grades" meant nothing.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.830
#1  Minase Runa

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:11.570
Thank you for buying
yet another H-Game.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.500
I'm adding an extra fee for bothering me,

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.230
so it's 230,000 yen.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.150
Right, right.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.580
6980 yen exactly.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:25.450
There's never anybody
in this shop but me.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.900
Don't worry.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:31.400
There's one other girl who's a regular.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.590
One?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.930
Are you gonna be okay
with so few customers?

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.200
What are you talking about?

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.600
That's why I work here.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.140
What's the point of studying
more than you already do?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.400
A stupid question.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.980
I have to be the best.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:46.970
Why?

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.370
Another stupid question.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:53.110
Do you need a reason to want
to best other people?

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.330
Hey, Minase.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.950
If you're that smart,
why did you choose Hekiyou?

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:07.300
It appears you're judging me
on a misguided assumption.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.060
I'm not terribly bright.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.540
That's why I chose
Hekiyou to begin with,

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.920
and why I study so hard,

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.940
and why it makes me
happy to be number one.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.940
And that's why I think I'll be able
to keep getting perfect scores.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.210
And since I devote
all of my time to studying,

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.380
even if I do work here,

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.160
I'll never lose to someone

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.460
who buys time-consuming games,

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:42.760
or who takes extra part-time jobs
to pay for those expensive games,

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:47.600
or who spends more time
with others than is necessary.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:07.280
I won't be able to beat her unless
I'm totally devoted, huh?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.450
But I want to win.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.550
I want to beat Minase.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:15.810
I want to win!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.780
I want to win!

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.870
I doubled the amount of
time I spent studying.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:34.250
Even so, I kept up with my classmates,

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:35.820
and my jobs.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.040
Of course, I played games every day.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:43.030
I didn't just want to be smart.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.990
I wanted to be like
the hero in my games,

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.290
who could make all the
pretty girls happy.

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:52.510
But eventually, it caught up with me...

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:58.040
And part of me was ready to
give up on the special slot.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.360
Okay, last round!

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.320
This time, I'm getting
out of last place!

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.880
It won't be that easy, Mamoru.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.760
You can keep giving me your

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.470
best cards for the rest of your life.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:10.550
Damn it!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.260
Excuse me, guys.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.420
What's wrong?

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.400
Well, you know...

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.090
The time you spend with your
classmates is very important...

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.290
You're wasting your time.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.040
That's not true.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.720
You can't be all work and no play...

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.860
Escapism.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.960
You're trying to escape reality.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.520
Did you hear me, Minase?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.810
The time you spend with your
classmates is very important...

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.310
Congratulations on getting the
7th best score in our grade.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:41.490
That's a very specific
estimate of where I'll be...

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.800
If you want to take the
special slot from me,

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.590
you're going to have to use
all of your time to do it.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.590
I...

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:53.380
I've decided I'm not going
to give up on anything

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.590
I want to do, and still
make the special slot!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.670
It doesn't matter.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:02.340
It doesn't affect me in the least
how you choose to live your life.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.470
You, who'll have the 9th best score.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.840
9th...

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.970
It went down a little.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:12.120
Minase! Let me have the special slot!

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:15.780
Sugisaki-kun, I understand
that you want

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:19.120
to be more than just a smart person.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.570
But are you sure you're going
about it the right way?

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.040
I can see your underwear.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:31.710
I suppose it can't be helped.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:37.870
Why, I wonder?

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:44.000
A part of me still
wanted to beat Minase.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:50.310
Oh, you haven't given up on
the special slot, Sugisaki?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.380
You don't have to tell me.
I can guess by watching you.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.600
I see.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.630
It's fun playing with you guys,

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.350
but there's someone else
I'd like to play with.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:02.480
So I won't be able to spend
as much time with you...

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.450
Sugisaki.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.370
Math's the one subject
I'm really good at,

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.960
so I could teach you, if you'd like.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:12.770
I think I could teach you
Japanese, if you wanted.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.590
I could teach you English.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:19.490
I think I'm the best at school
when it comes to Modern History.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.870
The girls in the chemistry
club will help, too.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.280
Okay.

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:26.080
Let's have a meeting to discuss how

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.790
we're going to help Sugisaki
study for finals.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:32.830
All right.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.850
Okay, Sugisaki.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.070
Let's get started.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.550
What's with you guys?

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:40.300
You're just teasing me for
trying to get the special slot.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:41.870
See, Minase?

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.690
Maybe what I've done
hasn't been a waste.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:47.280
After school, he and I will study together.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.670
Study what?

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.530
Then finally...

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.830
Good morning, Minase.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.210
Good morning, Sugisaki-kun.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:15:00.050
Sorry to have you come
so early, Minase.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:01.220
As you should be.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:05.570
Test results aren't something you
should share with another person.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.740
Well, that's true...

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:08.230
See?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.730
They're putting up the results now.

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.790
You should go look at
them on your own.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:14.860
Sure, but...

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.060
It doesn't matter.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.750
Let's just go see.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.020
Congratulations on getting 9th place.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.080
Hanai Naomi

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.550
I did not!

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.090
I'd guessed you'd be around nine.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.300
You guessed?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.470
Then seven.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.360
Daichi Nozawa

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.010
Guess not.

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:42.360
Don't scare me...

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.650
Well then...

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.620
Minatsu Shiina
Ijuuin Youko
Morino Nanako

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.810
As of four, I haven't seen your name.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.890
Does that mean you're higher up?

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:52.360
Yamauchi

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.640
Not three....

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:55.140
Or two.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.640
No way...

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.780
Did I not even make the top 10?

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:05.230
Minase Runa

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.090
Minase is number one...

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:15.360
I didn't expect this to happen.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:19.300
Did you think you'd lose?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.540
Huh?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.670
What are you talking about?

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.070
Look closer.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.870
#1 Sugisaki Ken

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.060
What's with the delayed reaction?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.170
Minase, I got a perfect score!

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.850
It looks like I got a perfect score!

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:50.950
It does.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:52.070
I'm surprised.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.070
W-What should I do?

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.830
Why don't you start by running up to

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.930
the roof and taking a dive into the sky?

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.520
Of course!

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.230
That's just what I feel like doing!

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.020
I'll be back!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.350
That would kill me!

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:11.080
I think there's a problem
with your reaction time.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.580
Anyway, I did it!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.520
I beat you and I get
the special slot...

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:18.530
No, you didn't beat me.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.270
What happens now?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.120
Two people with the top score...

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.740
Has that ever happened before?

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.870
I never said anything about

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.100
wanting the special slot, you know.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:35.870
Excuse me, then.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.630
Because of the way she said it,

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:44.060
I never did feel like I beat Minase.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:49.760
But as a result, I was
given the special slot.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.930
And in the spring of the next year...

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:58.170
Student Council Room

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:00.050
What are you doing, Aka-chan?

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:00.570
Student Council Room

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.300
I can't reach!

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:05.180
I'll put these away for you.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.800
I'll help, too!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:13.310
What are you doing there?

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:15.950
You're just expelling extra carbon dioxide.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.740
It's time for my first
student council meeting.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:19.790
I see.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.080
You're preparing for all four
girls to yell "Creep!"

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.190
Why would I be preparing for that?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:30.190
I was just thinking about what my
first words to them should be.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:33.630
"I'm quitting the Student Council."

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.660
That's a bit too sudden!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.030
Goodbye, then.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.000
Don't leave when I'm shouting at you!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.510
Act as you did with me.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:48.770
Why not act as you did with me,
and shout some silly goal like an idiot?

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:54.790
Girls like guys like that.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:55.650
Goodbye.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.520
Hey, Minase!

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:02.530
A goal, huh?

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.450
My goal is...

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.530
Go play a love sim!

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.730
What you lack, you know, is a
main character's mentality.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:12.940
Look at the heroes in those games!

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.560
All the girls love them,

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:16.170
and they make everyone happy, right?

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.550
You should try to be like that!

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:21.750
The one who gave me a
chance to change...

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.990
Somebody who's trying to be like me

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:27.050
doesn't have the right to
join the student council.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.200
The one who gave me the
power to keep going.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:33.710
The wounds in your heart...

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:38.170
Even if you think they've healed,
most of the time, they haven't.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.550
Once in a while, you have
to let your feelings out.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.710
The one who helped me when
I was pushing myself too hard.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:48.580
And...

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.340
Um, are you okay?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.690
The one who made me decide to be

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.350
a man who could protect a girl.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.930
The harem route, where I

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:07.630
make all the girls of the
Student Council happy.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:12.630
To be a man who can
make many girls happy.

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:15.300
That's my...

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.360
I love you all!

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.630
I really love you!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:22.900
Everyone, date me and
I'll make you all happy!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:24.980
Jeez.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:30.880
Why must we listen to a long
story about Sugisaki's past?

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:32.850
Seriously.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:36.250
I was so bored I fell asleep.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.990
You slept through
my awesome story?

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:40.690
It was a little long.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:45.410
They say speeches and
skirts are better short.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:46.500
Sounds good!

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.210
Watch it, Sugisaki.

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.110
The reason we had
Sugisaki tell us the

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.200
long story about what happened
before he joined the student

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.770
council is because we're
getting another anime.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:57.700
That's right.

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.420
We're trying to share what the

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.600
student council is like through
the past of Sugisaki Ken,

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:06.560
AKA Key-kun, the man who
writes the records for

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.290
the Hekiyou Academy Student Council.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.930
Well, I'm glad it's
getting animated, but

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.410
what about the title?

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.350
Should we change it?

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:15.490
That's right.

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:17.370
We need to put
something in the title or

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:20.130
nobody will know if it's
season one or two.

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.120
They could just watch.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:25.370
The characters and backgrounds
all have different designs.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:30.640
Well, that aside...

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.160
Y-Yeah.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:36.710
Then our new title will be
Student Council's Discretion Z!

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.400
Why Z?

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.150
Then what do you want, Sugisaki?

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:45.290
Um, maybe...

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.840
New Student Council's Discretion!

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:51.110
Too obvious!

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.770
Yours is no better than mine!

00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:56.650
Yeah... Maybe the problem is

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:59.480
we're putting too much emphasis
on the Student Council part?

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:02.310
I'd rather have a cooler title.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.060
All right.

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:05.410
Then what about this?

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.410
Crimson!

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.490
Sweet!

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:12.420
It <i>is</i> very cool,
but where does it come from?

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:14.420
Oh, it's <i>Kurimu's</i> Discreti<i>on</i>.

00:22:14.420 --> 00:22:16.690
So you shorten it to Crimson!

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:19.760
Thought so.

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:21.490
Miss President...

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:25.500
Don't look at me like that!

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:26.500
Oh, fine!

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:28.570
We'll do it like everyone else!

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:29.600
It's settled!

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:31.770
No complaints!

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.600
Anyway, it feels like we didn't
get a lot of screen time today.

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:07.330
Ken hogged it all.

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.850
I don't really think Key-kun's capable

00:24:09.850 --> 00:24:12.370
of carrying the story by himself.

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:16.110
Stop trying to stand
out so much, senpai.

00:24:17.290 --> 00:24:22.420
That's why I'd wanted to keep
that memorial in my heart.
